/**
 * src/lib/curriculum.ts — the "What You Will Learn" catalogue.
 *
 * Logos are REAL brand marks (Simple Icons, CC0), embedded as SVG path data so the page
 * makes zero third-party requests to render ~150 of them.
 *
 * Where `path` is null the brand is deliberately NOT drawn as a logo and falls back to a
 * branded lettermark. Two reasons: Microsoft withdrew its marks from the CC0 set on
 * trademark grounds (so Azure/Power Platform are lettermarks by necessity, not laziness),
 * and a few brands are too new to be in it. Items with no brand at all are concepts
 * (LoRA, KV-cache, hyperscaler setup) and were never going to have a logo.
 *
 * Generated — do not hand-edit; regenerate from the Simple Icons dataset.
 */

